imes 3d  collect-a-thons get bogged down in  worlds that are overly big and empty  if mario 64 received a graphical upgrade  similar to what super mario all-stars  did for the nes mario games  new camera controls and slightly less  clunky controls  i truly think it would modernize one of  gaming's biggest classics and be the  best way to introduce the game to an all  new generation  and look i know there was a nintendo ds  remaster back in 2004  but i'm talking about a complete  graphical and control overhaul  think about peach's castle from mario  odyssey but for  all of mario 64. just please don't make  it a limited release  nintendo chrono trigger is often  considered one of the greatest games of  all time  in fact it's my personal favorite game  of all time that is  why i have both of these that's just how  much i love this game  so do i think it needs a remake no  it's perfect as is the music is some of  the best in gaming the graphics are  charming and the gameplay is absolutely  spot on  that said it's also one of those games  that might eventually get lost to time  ironically given the time travel nature  of the game and that's the great thing  about remakes and remasters  as i mentioned at the beginning of this  video it introduces these properties to  an entirely new set of gamers  remakes with square enix are a bit of a  gamble  on one hand you might get this taken in  setsu 3 remake  which enhances the game in some ways but  is a detriment in others  you might get the secret of mana remake  which is well  better left not talked about or you  might get the final fantasy 7 treatment  which while different is a fantastic  game in its own right  and a loving tribute to the original  game chrono trigger deserves that love  and you know what i play chrono trigger  for the perfect game it is  if the game received the ff7 remake  treatment i'd still always have that  original game to play and i'd be excited  to see what new ways the game could be  remixed  like 