ng is 2d platform games are one  of the genres that can't really gain too  much from a 3d update  if anything it can risk destroying the  charm of those pixel graphics  but there was a 3d mega man game that  could  actually benefit from a modern remake  mega man legends  despite being relatively obscure for the  franchise the game is  charming and well deserving of more  attention  thanks to this qc look mega man legends  doesn't actually look  too terrible for playstation 1 era game  but imagine how the game could look with  modern cel-shaded graphics to enhance  its anime style  and while the gameplay was good in  concept it suffered from being one of  the first 3d console games  by today's standards controlling mega  man feels stiff and could definitely use  an  upgrade resident evil and silent hill  have long been considered to the best  survival horror  franchises and while resident evil has  thrived  both with fantastic remakes and  remasters that have managed to capture  the spirit of the original games  but with updated sensibilities as well  as great sequels that have been  generally well received by fans  sadly silent hill has had the opposite  fate  while silent hill 2 and 3 both received  hd remasters in 2012  silent hill 2's remake was completely  butchered  missing the atmospheric fog that was an  integral part of the game  the less said about those remakes the  better but as we've seen with the  resident evil franchise  horror games in particular benefit from  remakes with better sound and graphics  and the silent hill franchise truly is  deserving of this  while much of the horror of these games  is psychological a true visual upgrade  would only serve to enhance this  rather than detract from it ever since  the madness of abandon  which i covered in our video abandoned  in the silent hill conspiracy  there have been constant rumors of a new  silent hill game  konami announced a partnership earlier  this year with bloober team who  developed the medium and blair witch  which many have speculated could be to  create a new silent hill game  on the other hand there have also been  rumors that a reboot is already in the  works for silent hill  in the late 90s and early aughts teenage  rebellion took the form of  extreme sports punk music and elements  of hip-hop  while tony hawk pro skater excellently  incorporated this with its now well  beloved franchise  there was another game that resonated  with me even more  jet set radio just at radio and its  sequel  just at radio future sees you playing as  a rebel rollerblade gang  tagging the streets of tokyo too with  graffiti and escaping from the cops  while tony hawk was primarily about  seeing how many tricks you could combo  in a given time limit  chess set radio was unique in combining  these tricking elements alongside an  actual  objective of tagging the neighborhoods  of the game with rival gangs and the  cops acting as antagonists who could  actually hurt the player  meanwhile its sequel just set radio  feature increased the verticality of the  level design making every area a unique  trick fest  tony hawk pro skater oneplus 2 showed  that updating the style of game truly  does work  not only graphically but with new  elements and  the world of tokyo 2 deserves that kind  of treatment  around the same time the first smash  brothers game released to the n64  the dreamcast and arcades were getting  their very own unique 3d brawler  power stone power stone and power stone  2 were collectively 2  incredibly fun takes on the fighting  game genre while fighting games had gone  3d well before these games released  power stone made the entire arena part  of your arsenal with characters able to  pick up chairs  bombs and other weapons they could toss  at enemies or utilize  powerstone2 took this a step further  introducing four player matches  and moving interactive arenas that meant  these arenas weren't just background  flavor but each brought unique  challenges you 